   "id": "shabbat.112a.3",
   "daf": "112a",
   "sentenceId": 2,
   "he": "וְחוּטֵי סְבָכָה. פְּשִׁיטָא! לָא צְרִיכָא, דִּרְוִיחָא לַהּ. מַהוּ דְתֵימָא: מִישְׁלָף שָׁלְפָא לַהּ, קָא מַשְׁמַע לַן דְּאִשָּׁה חָסָה עַל שְׂעָרָהּ וּמִישְׁרָא שָׁרְיָא לַהּ.",
   "en": "We learned in the mishna: «And» a woman may tie the «strings of her hairnet» on Shabbat. The Gemara states: This is «obvious.» The Gemara clarifies the matter: «It was only necessary» to state this halakha in a case «where» the hairnet is tied «loosely on her» head. «Lest you say» that «she» sometimes «removes it» without untying it and the knots remain, «the mishna teaches us» that «a woman is protective of her hair» and avoids pulling it out, «and» therefore «she unties» the hairnet to avoid damaging her hair."
  }
 ],
